  "scope_of_acceptance": "Accepted means the unchanged registered checks passed. Static review findings outside that checker remain limitations and do not retroactively change the scores.",
  "validity_notes": [
    "Four pairs on one historical task are a small engineering panel, not evidence of broad model or briefing superiority.",
    "Both conditions receive the same complete instructions, task, source pin, tool restrictions, formatting normalization, and at most one external-check repair. The optional evidence is the intended difference.",
    "Costs are the final cumulative Claude CLI list-price estimates counted once, not verified subscription charges. Warmup and cold indexing are separate; machine and engineering costs are unmeasured.",
    "Recorded endpoint wall time includes source export and setup, the model session, external checks, executor-process shutdown, and measured warm briefing preparation for treatment. It excludes final candidate/artifact capture, scratch cleanup, and final result serialization.",
    "The secondary without-source-setup wall statistic removes the whole measured preparation bucket from both conditions and keeps warm briefing time. It is descriptive and does not replace the registered timing gate.",
    "Provider cache state and filesystem caches are uncontrolled. Tool counts and timing differences do not identify a causal mechanism by themselves.",
    "The frozen runner records file-byte changes, not chmod-only changes. The final patch review covers retained byte changes.",
    "The heldout preparation explicitly records probe_triggered=false. The analysis adapter therefore adds zero probe time; an absent probe flag or an unmeasured triggered probe stays unknown."
  ],
